## Out of scope, named and counted: `verification/probes/`

The scan's search root is `bench/` alone. `verification/probes/` holds **sixteen** files
in exactly this class — they open a real index and run raw SQL against `meta`,
`passages`, `passages_fts`:

    corpus-language-mix.mjs          keeping-diacritics-real-cost.mjs
    degenerate-real-index.mjs        lang_census.py
    diacritic-collision-cost.mjs     migrate-real-index.mjs
    droplist-adapts-to-corpus.mjs    scan-shape-v190-vs-fused.mjs
    expansion-penalties-probe.mjs    snippet-droplist-probe.mjs
    expansion-reach-probe.mjs        stoplist-cross-language.mjs
    folding-cost-and-benefit.mjs     vocab-scan-cost.mjs
    keeping-diacritics-cost.mjs      x4_probe_vocabulary.py

Counted, not estimated: the same predicates run over that root, with the identical run
over `bench/` as the positive control (it returns the 21-file inventory the merge request
records, the three newly-classified files included). A review of PR #232 reported fifteen;
the run above returns sixteen, and the list is what the number is.

Deferred rather than done, deliberately. Several of these are one-off instruments pinned
to the pre-rename generation the way `bench/vec_real_measure.mjs` is, so classifying them
is 0101's per-driver judgement made sixteen more times — its own exercise. Sixteen reasons
written in a hurry to keep a suite green would be sixteen bare names with a longer type,
which is precisely what `EXCUSED` exists against. `verification/probes/` is in the repo's
lint gate for the reason the Makefile states — a probe that produced a committed figure is
code we depend on — so extending the root is the right eventual move, taken as a decision
rather than as a rider.

No new ticket: ID allocation was collision-prone this session (`erg new` offered 0602 with
0599-0601 already on an open merge request), and this sits below the severity floor as
filed. Recording it here keeps it findable without minting an ID.

The scope claim is machine-checked meanwhile. `SEARCH_ROOT` and `UNSEARCHED_ROOT` are
module constants; `test_the_search_root_is_the_one_the_module_documents` fails if either
moves without the docstring, `test_the_inventory_stays_inside_the_search_root` fails if the
walk escapes, and `test_a_matching_file_outside_the_search_root_is_not_named` puts the same
driver byte-for-byte inside and outside the root and asserts only one is named. A widening
therefore reds three tests by name instead of silently changing what the module claims.

## Invariants

- No bench driver is modified: this ticket adds a guard and classifies, it does not
  change a measurement.
- 0101's curated exclusions survive as reasons rather than being discarded.
- The check stays pure Python — no `node`, no subprocess, no database — so it cannot
  skip.
- The derivation is not allowed to go vacuous: an empty vocabulary or an unparsed roster
  fails loudly rather than passing on nothing.
- The search root cannot widen silently: it is a constant with tests on it, so reaching
  `verification/probes/` is a deliberate edit that reds three named tests.

## Exit criteria

- [x] A derived-inventory scan names every bench file that opens a zoteus-built index.
- [x] Every file it names is rostered in `DRIVERS` or excused with a non-blank written
      reason; blank, absent and stale entries are each refused, each with a control.
- [x] The three files above are classified, with the reasoning in the docstring.
- [x] The red controls above are captured as terminal transcripts in the merge request,
      not paraphrased.
- [x] `make check` green and `./tickets/erg check tickets/` passes against
      `origin/main`'s ticket set.
- [x] The search root is a named constant, documented, and asserted — so the module
      cannot be read wider than it is.
